cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If ADA supports your work, please cite the software using this metadata."
title: "ADA: Automated Data Analyst"
type: software
version: "0.6.0"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
authors:
  - family-names: Nakra
    given-names: Sainesh
    website: "https://sainesh.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/saineshnakra/automated-data-analyst"
url: "https://automated-data-analyst.streamlit.app/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  ADA makes a paper's data audit, tables, figures and methods draft from research data and a
  plain study.yml, with every number traced to the data and a rebuild that can be verified. Every
  number is computed with pandas, SciPy and statsmodels and shown with its calculation, or refused
  with a reason. It also takes a first look at any CSV or Excel table, and works as a skill in
  Claude Code and Codex.
keywords:
  - data analysis
  - agent skill
  - Claude Code
  - Codex
  - reproducible research
  - publication figures
  - mixed models
  - exploratory data analysis
  - statistics
  - research data
  - business intelligence
  - automated data analysis
  - data visualization
  - Streamlit
  - CSV
  - Excel
